WEBVTT

00:03.120 --> 00:05.400
You're a valuable human resource.

00:05.400 --> 00:10.480
I would never do anything 
that might result in losing you.

00:11.880 --> 00:14.780
You understand that our interests align.

00:15.290 --> 00:18.620
That's why you've obeyed my orders.

00:19.120 --> 00:22.580
When you suspect I'm "pulling 
something" in spite of that,

00:22.970 --> 00:26.300
I'm only doing so for the sake
 of the larger picture.

00:26.980 --> 00:28.970
Let me repeat myself:

00:28.970 --> 00:34.160
I'm not your enemy, 
and I won't do anything to harm you.

00:34.160 --> 00:36.970
I don't need your faith or trust.

00:37.530 --> 00:41.930
For now, just understand that with your head.

02:16.720 --> 02:18.160
Get out already.

02:18.160 --> 02:20.910
Oh, I can't go anywhere until I heal up.

02:21.390 --> 02:23.200
I have broken bones, you know.

02:25.670 --> 02:28.080
Oh, that smarts.

02:28.080 --> 02:31.290
Dear me, what a mess you've made.

02:34.930 --> 02:36.550
This takes me back.

02:38.460 --> 02:42.640
To three years ago, when we first met.

02:44.720 --> 02:49.730
Eloquence 
and Silence

02:44.720 --> 02:49.730
Opening Act

02:56.880 --> 02:59.360
<i>A village on the Fifth Continent.</i>

02:59.360 --> 03:06.430
<i>Being so far from the Global Holy Church's 
headquarters on the First Continent,</i>

03:06.430 --> 03:09.040
<i>this place hasn't developed 
a magical civilization.</i>

03:09.620 --> 03:16.930
<i>A remote, utterly un-magical village 
in an ordinary, utterly un-magical country.</i>

03:18.570 --> 03:21.440
A coffin! Hey, that was a coffin, right?

03:21.440 --> 03:23.470
Yes, yes. I'm sure it was.

03:37.020 --> 03:38.940
<i>It couldn't be less remarkable.</i>

03:39.720 --> 03:42.530
<i>But a witch calls this village home.</i>

03:43.090 --> 03:46.480
<i>She's apparently lived here a long time,</i>

03:46.480 --> 03:50.130
<i>but until now, she's never caused a fuss.</i>

03:50.130 --> 03:53.630
<i>Which explains why her presence
 went unremarked upon.</i>

03:53.630 --> 03:56.170
<i>But lately, it's been one 
odd incident after another.</i>

03:57.870 --> 04:01.380
<i>And finally, the fuss drew attention.</i>

04:02.000 --> 04:07.220
<i>Now that this has happened, we must 
take the witch under our wing at once,</i>

04:07.670 --> 04:10.360
<i>before someone turns up dead.</i>

04:11.280 --> 04:12.200
Let's go.

04:25.650 --> 04:30.120
Well, this should do it for groceries. 
Do we have anything else to buy?

04:30.630 --> 04:33.330
Falvell, do you want anything?

04:36.040 --> 04:38.710
Aw, come on. Don't hold back.

04:38.710 --> 04:44.160
The latest batch of tea leaves and dyed stuff
were a hit, so the mayor paid us extra.

04:44.160 --> 04:47.090
Treat yourself once in a while.

04:47.860 --> 04:48.930
You there!

04:48.930 --> 04:50.030
What do you—

04:48.930 --> 04:50.890
Look what you've gone and done!

04:51.250 --> 04:53.040
My cows!

04:53.040 --> 04:55.000
Those were <i>my</i> cows!

04:55.000 --> 04:57.230
I don't know what you mean!
 We didn't touch them!

04:57.230 --> 05:01.150
Hey, lay off. We've got no proof,
 and the mayor's on her side.

05:01.150 --> 05:03.070
You'll catch hell if you try anything.

05:03.070 --> 05:05.980
Who else but a witch could've 
done something like that?!

05:05.980 --> 05:08.230
No human could've, that's for sure!

05:08.230 --> 05:10.660
A crazy witch must've done it!

05:12.240 --> 05:14.090
That's prejudice.

05:14.970 --> 05:17.790
Ideas like that belong 
in the past, if you ask me.

05:17.790 --> 05:19.120
Craig.

05:19.120 --> 05:21.750
This is about what happened 
two days ago, right?

05:22.890 --> 05:28.620
I didn't witness it myself, 
but I hear livestock fell from the sky.

05:28.620 --> 05:29.930
Hm? Huh?

05:31.090 --> 05:32.140
What the...

05:36.560 --> 05:39.670
That's right. And in pieces, too.

05:39.670 --> 05:42.320
Could a human do something like that?

05:42.320 --> 05:43.650
I doubt it.

05:44.140 --> 05:46.740
But the same goes for her.

05:47.100 --> 05:50.320
She couldn't do something like that
 in a million years, either.

05:50.320 --> 05:52.320
What?! But she's a witch!

05:52.320 --> 05:56.150
What makes this pair 
of monsters so different?!

05:56.640 --> 05:58.080
Hi there. Excuse me.

05:59.010 --> 06:02.470
I hate to butt in on a quarrel,

06:02.470 --> 06:05.020
but yours involves someone
 I came here to see,

06:05.020 --> 06:08.010
and your discussion piqued my interest.

06:08.460 --> 06:13.720
Why do you say that she, a witch,
 couldn't have done it?

06:14.120 --> 06:16.240
Wh-Who are you?

06:16.240 --> 06:19.920
Why? Because it's true.

06:19.920 --> 06:20.560
Oh?

06:21.040 --> 06:24.400
Everyone calls my big sister a witch,

06:24.400 --> 06:29.860
but Falvell Farmington 
can't cast a single spell!

06:30.100 --> 06:30.940
Well, now.

06:30.940 --> 06:35.080
What?! You expect me to believe she's 
innocent because she can't use magic?!

06:35.080 --> 06:37.140
Anyone can make an excuse like that!

06:37.140 --> 06:38.410
Not so loud.

06:39.010 --> 06:42.130
I'm afraid I must ask you to leave us.

06:52.120 --> 06:53.470
Put him down.

06:53.470 --> 06:54.170
Sure.

06:54.780 --> 06:56.810
Go home.

06:56.810 --> 06:57.540
Sure.

06:57.960 --> 06:59.000
All right.

07:00.890 --> 07:03.580
Oh, are you single?

07:03.580 --> 07:05.510
No, I've got a wife.

07:05.510 --> 07:06.360
Me, too.

07:06.750 --> 07:10.180
Is that so? Then shower them with love.

07:10.180 --> 07:12.570
Why not buy flowers for them on your way home?

07:12.980 --> 07:15.980
Good idea. I'll do that.

07:15.980 --> 07:17.330
Once in a while, you know?

07:18.630 --> 07:21.450
Was that... magic?

07:21.450 --> 07:23.380
Well, just a bit.

07:23.380 --> 07:26.690
Yikes! Magic gives me the creeps!

07:26.690 --> 07:29.360
Don't tell me <i>you're</i> behind everything?

07:31.870 --> 07:33.440
I wonder.

07:33.440 --> 07:35.620
Well, all joking aside...

07:35.620 --> 07:37.020
He passed it off as a joke!

07:37.750 --> 07:40.750
Lady Witch, I'd like a word.

07:41.160 --> 07:42.970
I've been looking for you.

07:43.900 --> 07:48.360
I'm Ashaf. A first-rate mage, as you saw.

07:48.930 --> 07:52.820
As you are a witch, 
I have an earnest request for you.

07:55.030 --> 07:56.460
Suspicious.

07:56.460 --> 07:58.620
You're super shady, Mister.

07:58.970 --> 08:04.830
But, well, you did help us out, 
so I guess we owe you a thank you.

08:10.220 --> 08:11.890
Hey, watch it.

08:11.890 --> 08:13.100
You just jostled me.

08:14.240 --> 08:15.720
Are you listening?

08:43.500 --> 08:44.930
Really, now?

08:53.970 --> 08:58.140
I never thought I'd need <i>three</i> layers 
against a flesh-and-blood opponent.

08:59.260 --> 09:00.850
Move! You're in my way!

09:00.850 --> 09:05.060
How fierce. What exactly 
am I stopping you from doing?

09:05.470 --> 09:07.820
Hand over that witch.

09:07.820 --> 09:09.520
She's <i>my</i> prey.

09:09.920 --> 09:12.600
What's wrong with people today?

09:12.600 --> 09:15.240
What do you all want with Falvell?!

09:17.380 --> 09:18.660
Remember this face?

09:19.160 --> 09:21.740
Or this mark?!

09:22.240 --> 09:23.580
That mark...

09:25.340 --> 09:27.050
Sounds like a yes.

09:43.020 --> 09:45.050
What's this freaky thing?

09:46.930 --> 09:47.950
It vanished.

09:49.770 --> 09:51.610
<i>Did it protect her?</i>

09:54.000 --> 09:55.650
Did you see that?

09:55.650 --> 09:57.900
What was that monster just now?

09:57.900 --> 09:59.590
There she is.

09:59.590 --> 10:01.970
The witch! The witch is right there!

10:01.970 --> 10:03.620
Then that monster was...

10:03.620 --> 10:05.890
Not good. People saw that.

10:05.890 --> 10:07.210
What?

10:07.210 --> 10:09.320
No. You're wrong!

10:09.320 --> 10:10.960
Falvell didn't do anything!

10:11.480 --> 10:13.350
She didn't!

10:32.440 --> 10:33.730
We don't have parents.

10:34.150 --> 10:37.760
The villagers don't treat us like people,

10:37.760 --> 10:40.610
but the mayor's always been good to us.

10:41.040 --> 10:47.680
Falvell uses plants from our garden and 
the mountain out back for dyeing and tea,

10:47.680 --> 10:50.960
and the mayor sells what 
she makes to acquaintances.

10:51.370 --> 10:52.670
Her stuff's popular.

11:07.200 --> 11:08.230
Well, I'll be.

11:08.230 --> 11:10.680
Hard to believe how good it tastes, right?

11:10.680 --> 11:14.060
It's the best tea I've ever had.

11:14.340 --> 11:18.780
She can't use magic, but she says this is 
part of the witch knowledge she inherited.

11:19.520 --> 11:20.620
I see.

11:21.310 --> 11:23.160
Would you care for a cup, too?

11:23.600 --> 11:25.120
It tastes wonderful.

11:30.770 --> 11:32.000
What a surprise.

11:32.600 --> 11:37.270
I expected you to scream at me to 
undo the spell, but you've stayed calm.

11:37.270 --> 11:39.210
I guess you don't like to waste effort.

11:39.660 --> 11:43.300
And I examined you 
while you were unconscious,

11:43.720 --> 11:47.070
but I found no signs
 of magical enhancement.

11:47.070 --> 11:53.090
Yet you're tough enough to have barely 
a scratch on you. And that brute strength...

11:53.090 --> 11:55.770
You don't strike me as an ordinary human.

11:58.070 --> 11:59.890
That mark on your neck.

12:00.370 --> 12:03.320
It proves you're under 
a witch's curse, doesn't it?

12:04.460 --> 12:06.280
A witch's curse?

12:06.280 --> 12:12.620
If my guess isn't wrong, you hoped 
she'd give you a clue about the caster.

12:12.620 --> 12:17.100
Or you suspect her of 
casting the curse herself.

12:18.260 --> 12:20.600
Why don't we start there?

12:21.580 --> 12:25.580
But first, may I have a second cup?

12:27.820 --> 12:30.890
Now, let me see. You are?

12:30.890 --> 12:33.120
My name? Owent.

12:33.120 --> 12:35.200
It's a pleasure, Owent.

12:35.200 --> 12:36.770
I'd like your confirmation.

12:37.180 --> 12:39.760
Falvell can't speak, can she?

12:39.760 --> 12:41.700
No, she can't.

12:41.700 --> 12:44.740
Not a single "witch" in our family ever can.

12:45.050 --> 12:47.520
They can't even make 
noises in their throats.

12:47.520 --> 12:50.620
What? You told me she was sick.

12:50.620 --> 12:53.260
Well, I mean, it's a weird story, right?

12:53.260 --> 12:57.870
We just saw so many crazy things 
that I figured I might as well come clean.

12:58.870 --> 13:02.590
I see. And as such, she can't cast spells.

13:03.140 --> 13:05.590
How much do you all know about magic?

13:05.590 --> 13:06.540
Not much...

13:07.090 --> 13:08.060
Thank you.

13:09.120 --> 13:11.680
In that case, time for a lesson.

13:12.560 --> 13:15.290
Generally speaking,

13:15.290 --> 13:21.020
a person with magical energy 
casts spells by tracing runes.

13:21.440 --> 13:25.770
We either pour magic
 into pre-written runes,

13:25.770 --> 13:29.410
or write runes using magical energy itself.

13:37.160 --> 13:38.540
Let me treat you.

13:40.000 --> 13:41.370
Listen, asshole—

13:46.330 --> 13:47.990
She froze up?

13:47.990 --> 13:50.160
Well, anyway...

13:50.160 --> 13:53.140
As you can see, 
writing forms the basis of magic.

13:53.600 --> 13:57.480
Spellcasting relies on 
special letters called "runes."

13:57.480 --> 13:59.450
But there are exceptions.

13:59.920 --> 14:04.150
And Falvell, I suspect your 
bloodline is one of them.

14:05.430 --> 14:09.470
Its Origin: the "Mystic Witch,"
 Luna Farmington.

14:10.160 --> 14:15.410
A practitioner of vocative magic
who cast all her spells with speech.

14:10.660 --> 14:16.910
<b>Invocation</b>

14:17.350 --> 14:23.010
But since you can't use your voice, 
you naturally can't cast spells, either.

14:24.340 --> 14:25.990
For real?

14:25.990 --> 14:27.730
You sure know a lot.

14:27.730 --> 14:31.550
Do all mages know so much about witches?

14:31.550 --> 14:33.520
I don't believe so.

14:33.520 --> 14:38.360
Very few have knowledge of 
the Mystic Witch, in particular.

14:39.090 --> 14:40.160
Well?

14:40.160 --> 14:41.190
Huh?

14:41.450 --> 14:44.380
Falvell descends from the Mystic Witch.

14:44.380 --> 14:47.070
Does that match the witch who cursed you?

14:47.490 --> 14:51.030
Being a different bloodline 
doesn't prove shit.

14:51.400 --> 14:53.990
That bitch swaps bodies.

14:55.580 --> 14:56.830
Oh?

14:56.830 --> 14:59.540
And you're telling me she can't use magic?

14:59.920 --> 15:03.130
What do you call that thing 
that sent me flying, then?!

15:03.130 --> 15:05.520
Yes, that's the problem.

15:05.520 --> 15:08.010
I'm not saying it presents a contradiction.

15:08.410 --> 15:12.090
The problem is that we may have enemies here.

15:12.450 --> 15:17.310
That thing looked exactly 
as though Falvell created it.

15:17.880 --> 15:21.230
But Falvell can't use magic.

15:21.230 --> 15:23.600
Working from that assumption,

15:23.600 --> 15:27.610
someone must have orchestrated 
it to appear that way.

15:27.970 --> 15:33.030
Now that so many people have seen it,
 if any more incidents occur,

15:33.030 --> 15:36.610
all the blame will fall upon the "wicked witch."

15:38.000 --> 15:41.840
Just to check, are there 
any local spellcasters?

15:41.840 --> 15:43.710
No. Not even one.

15:44.200 --> 15:48.650
I hear these minor odd incidents
started about a month ago.

15:48.650 --> 15:51.530
Did any outsiders come through around then?

15:51.530 --> 15:53.620
Not really.

15:53.620 --> 15:57.180
Well, I guess I might count.

15:58.180 --> 16:01.000
My dad and I moved here half a year ago.

16:01.610 --> 16:05.190
Of course, neither of us can do magic, though.

16:05.190 --> 16:08.160
Craig and his dad help us out!

16:08.780 --> 16:12.550
They protect us like the mayor does!

16:12.550 --> 16:15.320
No need to be so protective.

16:16.260 --> 16:18.700
I won't pounce on every suspect I find.

16:19.080 --> 16:22.120
Half a year is too long ago. 
He's in the clear.

16:22.120 --> 16:24.880
Hmm... No clues, then.

16:25.470 --> 16:27.980
Our guest still doesn't 
seem convinced, either.

16:30.370 --> 16:31.410
Are you scared?

16:32.540 --> 16:39.090
A bestial woman, 
a mysterious mage, the villagers...

16:39.090 --> 16:42.950
You and your brother are 
surrounded by too many enemies.

16:42.950 --> 16:45.020
Do you have to spell it out like that?

16:47.040 --> 16:51.860
Don't worry. I've come to 
protect you two from now on.

16:54.750 --> 16:56.320
Let me reintroduce myself.

16:56.940 --> 17:02.600
I come from an occult organization 
of magic, by magic, and for magic:

17:02.600 --> 17:05.290
the Order of Magical Resonance.

17:05.980 --> 17:10.190
Lady Witch, would you return 
to the Order with me?

17:18.200 --> 17:19.700
I'm back.

17:20.230 --> 17:21.850
You're home late.

17:23.840 --> 17:27.380
Hey! Are you drinking Falvell's tea again?

17:27.380 --> 17:28.990
That's the last of it.

17:29.650 --> 17:33.010
It's just so good, I can't help it.

17:34.250 --> 17:36.360
Good thing I got some more.

17:36.360 --> 17:39.570
Oh, that should keep us for a while.

17:39.950 --> 17:43.160
Falvell ought to start charging us already.

17:43.480 --> 17:46.050
We pay her, just not with money.

17:47.090 --> 17:49.130
Oh, you won't believe what happened today.

17:51.830 --> 17:53.090
What do you think?

17:54.080 --> 17:58.180
I've never seriously 
considered leaving the village.

17:58.920 --> 18:00.800
It doesn't feel real.

18:01.120 --> 18:05.070
I mean, can <i>you</i> imagine 
this hell ever ending?

18:05.730 --> 18:09.690
Then again, what's to say things 
will get better if we go?

18:10.080 --> 18:12.230
To start with, that guy's really shady.

18:12.540 --> 18:14.420
I don't trust a word he says.

18:15.140 --> 18:16.990
I'll come back tomorrow.

18:18.340 --> 18:22.080
Don't worry. We're used 
to having lots of enemies.

18:22.540 --> 18:24.590
This is nothing new.

18:24.590 --> 18:26.400
We can get by somehow.

18:28.250 --> 18:29.820
Just like we always have.

18:31.180 --> 18:34.300
It's all just like always.

18:38.040 --> 18:39.220
Hey, Falvell...

18:40.300 --> 18:43.430
Do you trust him? That Ashaf guy?

18:47.770 --> 18:50.470
Yeah. You're right.

18:50.470 --> 18:53.850
Okay! I'll whip up something 
extra tasty tonight!

18:56.130 --> 18:57.940
You can't understand it?

18:58.290 --> 19:00.280
Sheltering a witch, you mean?

19:00.870 --> 19:05.020
A witch with no magic is just dead weight.

19:05.590 --> 19:07.500
What do you want her for?

19:07.500 --> 19:12.100
Oh, so you believe she can't cast spells now?

19:12.550 --> 19:17.510
If I see someone up close long enough, I can 
tell if she's that bitch or not on the inside.

19:17.510 --> 19:20.970
Is that so? I'm glad she's 
been cleared of suspicion.

19:21.510 --> 19:24.430
But I wouldn't call her "dead weight."

19:25.030 --> 19:29.560
Do you remember how she 
reacted to seeing your mark?

19:30.160 --> 19:32.800
It clearly rang a bell.

19:34.560 --> 19:36.070
You forgot?

19:36.480 --> 19:39.920
Maybe the hit that sent you flying 
knocked a few memories loose, too.

19:40.740 --> 19:44.700
If you ask me, we shouldn't 
be surprised she recognized it.

19:45.380 --> 19:50.300
She probably has a similar mark 
somewhere on her own body.

19:50.890 --> 19:52.540
Don't you find it strange?

19:53.220 --> 19:55.860
Her voice is the source of her magic.

19:55.860 --> 19:59.770
Generations of witches, 
and only witches, losing their voices

19:59.770 --> 20:01.760
couldn't be more contrived.

20:02.310 --> 20:06.220
So, could she be under a type of curse, too?

20:08.190 --> 20:10.950
Vocative magic boasts unparalleled power.

20:11.470 --> 20:16.610
Perhaps another witch got scared 
and sealed it away with a curse.

20:16.610 --> 20:20.580
So what? That makes her even more useless.

20:20.580 --> 20:22.890
A witch's curse is a pain in the—

20:22.890 --> 20:24.670
True, it is a nuisance.

20:24.670 --> 20:26.820
Undoing curses is a challenge.

20:27.320 --> 20:31.790
Or it would be, if there 
were only two ways to do it.

20:32.750 --> 20:35.240
Hey! What do you know about—

20:34.270 --> 20:35.240
Not now.

20:36.310 --> 20:38.380
I hear a commotion across the way.

20:42.380 --> 20:43.240
Craig!

20:44.640 --> 20:47.660
What's all the fuss? What happened?

20:47.660 --> 20:48.680
It came back!

20:48.680 --> 20:50.760
That monster showed up again!

20:51.260 --> 20:53.140
And then, the mayor...

20:53.690 --> 20:54.950
How gruesome.

20:54.950 --> 20:57.280
Her greatest benefactor, of all people.

20:57.280 --> 20:59.110
Then we were right all along.

20:59.110 --> 21:00.980
That girl is a devil.

21:00.980 --> 21:02.820
We can't leave her alive!

21:03.080 --> 21:04.990
And it gets worse!

21:04.990 --> 21:11.410
An "expert witch hunter" showed up 
and led the villagers to Falvell's house!

21:11.410 --> 21:13.790
He had this weird mask on and...

21:22.960 --> 21:24.130
An Executioner!

21:24.130 --> 21:25.760
This really is bad news!

21:25.760 --> 21:26.590
I'll go with you!

21:27.620 --> 21:28.740
That makes twice.

21:36.910 --> 21:39.610
Executioners work in pairs.

21:40.040 --> 21:42.570
I take it you're one of them.

21:45.890 --> 21:51.240
That's all the proof you 
needed to pull the trigger?

21:53.770 --> 21:55.310
You said you'd cleared me,

21:57.000 --> 21:59.690
but you suspected me this whole time.

22:00.720 --> 22:02.470
Adults don't play fair.

22:19.210 --> 22:20.520
What?

24:01.000 --> 24:04.290
I want to teach you what love is.

24:05.800 --> 24:09.960
Next time: "Eloquence 
and Silence: Final Act."

24:06.670 --> 24:09.960
Eloquence and Silence

24:06.670 --> 24:09.960
Final Act
